## Writing Rules

Rules implement the `asentric.Rule` interface:

```go
package rules

import (
    "github.com/asentric/asentric/pkg/asentric"
    "github.com/asentric/asentric/pkg/utils"
)

type MyRule struct{}

func (r *MyRule) Name() string { 
    return "my-rule" 
}

func (r *MyRule) Severity() asentric.Severity { 
    return asentric.SeverityMedium 
}

func (r *MyRule) Evaluate(ctx asentric.Context) (*asentric.Alert, error) {
    for _, log := range ctx.Logs() {
        if log.Event.Name == "Transfer" {
            from := utils.GetFieldString(log.Event.Fields, "from")
            if utils.IsZeroAddress(from) {
                return asentric.NewAlert(
                    r.Name(), 
                    "Mint Detected", 
                    r.Severity(),
                ), nil
            }
        }
    }
    return nil, nil
}
```

Register rules in `cmd/watcher/main.go`:

```go
engine.RegisterRule(&rules.MyRule{})
```

### Built-in Rules

The SDK provides several built-in rules you can use:

- `rules.NewERC20DefaultRule()` - Detects all ERC20 Transfer/Mint/Burn events (value > 100)
- `rules.NewERC20TransferRule(cfg)` - Detects Transfer events from a specific ERC20 contract
- `rules.NewLargeTransferRule()` - Detects large native token transfers
- `rules.NewWhaleAlertRule()` - Detects very large native token transfers

